sandbox/stubs/vendors/aws-amplify.ts's Auth.currentAuthenticatedUser() unconditionally resolved with a fake stub user, regardless of whether any sign-in had occurred. This made every fresh sandbox/test browser session look "already logged in" from first paint. Combined with ProtectedRoute -> useRedirectLoggedUser (in src/pages/Protected/hooks/) redirecting authenticated users to /my, and /my's useStepRedirect further redirecting incomplete-cart customers into /onboarding, this caused unauthenticated-prospect acceptance scenarios (e.g. "Sign Up - Select Plan") to non-deterministically race: fast automated DOM reads would see the Catalog page before the redirect fired, but a real user (or a slower run) would get redirected away into onboarding (e.g. Pick Number / Select Plan) instead of staying on /sign-up/.

While fixing this, also found a genuine latent bug in src/pages/Protected/hooks/useRedirectLoggedUser.ts: it awaited getUser() with no try/catch, assuming it resolves falsy when unauthenticated. Real Amplify's Auth.currentAuthenticatedUser() actually rejects when there's no session (confirmed by the sibling hook src/pages/SignIn/pages/SignIn/hooks/useRedirectLoggedUser.tsx, which correctly wraps the call in try/catch). This means real unauthenticated users hitting any Protected-guarded route could hit an unhandled promise rejection and get stuck on a permanent blank screen (isChecking never resolves to false). This may be a pre-existing production bug independent of the stub.